\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Products and derivatives}
\date{2026-11-03}


\p{In Schrödinger's equation the potential acts by multiplication,
#{\,(V\psi)(x)=V(x)\psi(x)}, and the momentum acts by differentiation.
Both are linear maps of one space of functions. Composing them in the
two orders, multiplying and then differentiating, or differentiating
and then multiplying, produces two different maps. The next definition
records the map that multiplies by a fixed function.}
